earn  from that experience don't put um our  future or our faith in another team  hands and um we gotta come off strong uh  really focus on this off season and then  um we're getting stronger getting ready  for the season and then obviously i  don't know what's going to happen with  otas and everything but when we are  allowed to get back together um really  focus and lock in and try to start off  right  you obviously have had a disappointing  season because of the injury what have  you learned the most about yourself  through the process of surgery rehab and  just not being able to do the thing you  love to do play football one i learned  i'm resilient  um you know you kind of think you are  and you kind of tell yourself you are  until a moment comes and and knocks you  knocks you on the ground um and you know  every single day i i know um how i'm  attacking it and i know my mindset and  trying to get one percent better every  single day with the help of my teammates  and help with trainers and patience you  know i'm a guy that always was trying to  go go go like let's go let's go and and  now you got to be smart especially  during the three hour process and um you  know it humbles you it humbles you you  know you got routine yourself how to  walk you gotta read you got you kind of  start you start starting square square  root you start from the floor all the  way up again um before you get all the  way up and stand up again so uh teaches  you it humbles you teaches you patients  and it shows that  i'm resilient not only am i saying i'm  brazilian i'm coming i'm showing myself  every day i'm having that um that  that battle i'm competing with myself um  every single day so far  saquon tell us how that experience turns  into  something tangible something positive  that you can use  to be a better player  when the time comes for you to put the  uniform on and go out there and carry  the football again well you get to see  the field differently  um watch it on tv or or watching it from  the stands or watching it from the uh  up in the booth you can see the the game  different um you have a different  appreciation of it uh just because it's  been taken away from you  and you know you you're forced to work  on things that you may have not worked  on before um you know you always say you  focus on the little things on the little  things but um you know you might just be  focusing you might be thinking you're  focusing on the little things and  attacking the weight room but you only  focus on all the big muscles you're not  focusing on all the little muscles that  that have a  a a key impact on how you are as an  athlete so um for me uh we're starting  from from ground zero all the way back  up um just focusing on the little things  and the things that i wasn't as good at  before um injury and try to improve that  and make that a strength and hopefully  whenever that time is again i'm on the  field  i can i can show that  i saw that you said recently that you  plan to do some workouts with otto  beckham jr he's obviously going through  the same thing how helpful is that to  have someone that you can compare notes  with right now real time not somebody  who did it last year the year before but  somebody who's doing it right now how  much does that help you yeah it  definitely helps i mean it helps to have  anyone that experiences injury um  whether i'm talking to  ap or even you know one of my college  buddy mark who tours acl um in college  and having conversations with him but oh  you know especially  someone that you know we respect each  other games but not only we respect each  other's games but we're really good  friends and um to be able to link up and  and have rehab together for a little bit  i think this is going to benefit both of  us  adrian peterson's the ultimate example  my goodness he tore his on christmas eve  and he was good to go week one the next  year and almost set the single season  rushing record what's he told you to do  and and to to how to handle this going  forward  um he told me you're gonna you're gonna  find out that you're gonna come better  from this um  wherever it's not just only football  but off the field whether it's in your  life  whether it's mentally  but also in football you become better  than this because you are  focusing you're forced to to train  muscles that you may have not been  training um as much as you should have  in the past um and you just get a  different understanding of the  understanding of your body um so for me  it was just asking a lot of questions uh  with the doctors and the trainers and  then and seeing where you know the the  steps that they want me to take um and  how much they want to improve and and  attacking it and you gotta attack it but  you gotta tackle smarter and that's  something that he told me and um i'm  very fortunate to be able to have a guy  like that that i can reach out and call  at any single time and know exactly  where he was throughout his uh his rehab  process  we just finished covering a hiring cycle  of seven new nfl head coaches just a  year ago joe judge was one of the new  hires there's still a lot of people that  don't really know what to make of joe  judge and what kind of a coach he's  going to be how would you describe your  head coach to someone who doesn't know  him  um he's a guy that's going to come in  here and get the best out of all his  players um and it's not just from what  he's going to say he's going to show it  and he's going to get the best out  you're going to push you um you know  when you come to work every single day  you're going to find something that  you're going to get better  whether it's on the football field or  whether it's in the playbook or whether  it's just understanding of the game as a  whole um you know  even if you you may be a well-known  running back but you're going to know  special teams um you may be a well-known  quarterback for you on those special  teams you're going to know you're going  no defense going no special teams but we  all gonna know uh what we got to do  because at the end of the day football  is a complimentary game and that's the  kind of coach that um i don't think i  know that we have um and i'm very  excited i wish um obviously i i could  have done a little bit more this year  but  hopefully next year when i'm able to get  back with the team  you know hopefully we can show everyone  what we really got  you've got three years in your nfl  career and you've shown that you can be  among the very best nfl running backs  the windows open for a second contract  you and the team have any understanding  about  when that's going to happen is there  going to be negotiation this off season  or does everybody just kind of want to  wait and see what happens in 2021 um to  be honest uh  that's at least my worries and then  that's claiming on my mind right now um  to even have that conversation spark  that conversation up i'm really just  focusing on uh you know getting getting  this knee ready um  because you know i want to be the best  player that i can be hopefully better  than i ever was for near johns  well one of the benefits of being a  great player opportunities to make money  elsewhere such as being a spokesman for  oikos tell us what you have going on  with them  yeah oikos they're coming out with a  commercial going super ball uh the pro  face commercial um and the pro face kind  of just stands for uh what will you do  as an athlete or or a trainer or or  anyone who goes in in a weight room it's  that face that you make when you're  grinding when you're showing that raw  emotion that attention motion where  you're trying to set a pr record uh in  the weight room whether it's bench  weather squat um so that that's adobo  concept that i believe that they came up  with and i would say they're also doing  a program for trainers  in america where  you are able to  sign up to originalsproforpros.com  as a trainer  and be able to get profits 100 profits  actually  in february uh whoever was able to to  donate and then also up to a thousand  dollars um for trainers so especially  what's going on in this world and the  pandemic i think that's very cool uh  what oracle's doing and i'm happy and  proud to be able to say that i'm a line  and partnering up with them all right  you got to show us your face then what's  your face what's your pr face  oh man don't put me on the spot uh  my face the best thing i say uh you i  think uh i believe it's on super bowl  but uh you'll be able to see it on the  screen  hey uh chris godwin your former teammate  at penn state's going for a super bowl  ring are you pulling for one team or the  other you know you got friendships all  throughout the league who are you who  are you rooting for in this game coming  up on sunday um not real for anyone i  know uh i wish i do wish the best for uh  for rod uh for chris godwin and um but i  think it would be cool for tom brady to  get his seventh ring um  so i would say i probably if i had to  pick  uh which i've been forced to pick a  couple of times i i would say i'm  picking up brady in the bucks  all right well hey say quan it's great  talking to you we wish you all the best  we look forward to seeing you back on  the field we look forward to see that  face the commercial coming up during the  game on sunday thanks pal thank you  thank you  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

